# A sibling nested method of a factory reads a host own field through `node`;
# the returned method calls it. The field's value at the return (3) lives in
# the copied context C at the field's body-part ordinal, the sibling's node.
# Exit 7 on the correct value; 81 is the program's own refusal.
fn: makeOuter (int: n) fn: () int
    int: third 3
    fn: helper () int
        return: node\third
    fn: inner () int
        return: helper()
    return: inner
@: held makeOuter(7)
int: got held()
int: ok 7
if: got != 3
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
